  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1205 AM MST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nFor Friday, temps will cool somewhat as cooler air advects in from \nthe east. Additionally, we will see quite a bit more clouds by \nafternoon across  the entire region. Expect max temps in the 60 to \n65F range, with mid 50s valleys. some showers could develop Friday \nevening across the San Juans.\n\nSaturday...Temperatures continue to cool off region-wide. Expect max \ntemps over the plains to be in the 55 to 60F range with U40s \nvalleys. Lots of clouds across the entire area are expected. \n\nOver the San Juans, the best chance of mainly snow will occur during \nthe daylight hours Saturday. Snow is expected for the entire period \na pass level, with (only) several inches of snow expected over the \nSW mtns. Snow levels will be in the 8500 range during the day with \nvalues falling to 8000 feet by the Saturday evening hours. Overall \nabout 12 hours of precip are anticipated over the SW mtns with only \nabout 0.30 inches of precip anticipated.\n\nThe best chance for precip over the plains will be Saturday evening, \nwith overall best pops at lower elevations over the far SE Plains. \n\nSunday...Morning showers plains then clearing. mountains should be \ndry during the daylight hours. Temps will be in the 60s most areas. \n\nMonday will be dry with temps warming into the 50s.\n\nFor Tuesday, a more significant storm will move into the region, \nwith precip developing along the CONTDVD by later in the afternoon. \nAt this time this storm will have the highest impacts across the \nDivide (especially San JUans), and possibly parts of the Pikes Peak \nregion (including N El Paso county). \n\nFor the rest of the week, things appear unsettled. as a strong jet \nwill be over the state during this period. How much impactful \nweather we get later in the week will depend on how that jetstream \ntracks over the region. The farther south the jet tracks the better \nchance of precip we will see, especially over the mtns and\npossibly the plains. \\/Hodanish",
